      "artist": "Gerry Dincher from Hope Mills, NC",
      "description": "The market house in Fayetteville, North Carolina was built in 1832. It was declared a National Historic Landmark in 1973. It was burned by protestors in the wake of the death of George Floyd in 2020. There is a movement in the community to tear it down while others are fighting to preserve it. It stands in downtown Fayetteville in the Cool Springs District.The windows were broken, now boarded. It is fenced off to keep people out. Damage to the structure was superficial.",
